cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scIntegrate, please cite it."
title: "scIntegrate: is integration needed, which method, and one object carrying the answer"
abstract: >-
  scIntegrate compares single-cell integration methods including the un-integrated baseline,
  measures mixing per cell type against chance for that population's own batch composition,
  benchmarks with scIB, names a default embedding, and states separately - computed from the
  experimental design - what that embedding may be used for.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jiaen
    family-names: Lin
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JiaenLin/scIntegrate"
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - integration
  - batch-effect
  - scIB
  - scVI
